{"authored" [{"question" "q-35965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $Q(-3,3,3)$ and parallel to $v=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $Q$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=q+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $Q$ is $q=⟨-3,3,3⟩.$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨-3,3,3⟩+t⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨-3,3,3⟩+t⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨-3,3,3⟩+⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨-5,3,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}⟩+t⟨3,3,-3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨3,-3,3⟩+t⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},3,-5⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩+t⟨-3,3,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨-3,3,3⟩+t⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $K(-4,-3,-1)$ and $L(1,2,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $K$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=k+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $k$ is the position vector of $K.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $K(-4,-3,-1)$ and $L(1,2,4),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{KL} \\\\  & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨-4,-3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/