"basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,1,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,-1,5⟩.$ Find all the possible points $Q$ on that line such that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $Q$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩)-⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨1,-1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+(-t)^{2}+(5t)^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{27{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\pm 3\\sqrt{3}t & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{1}}=⟨1,1,1⟩+⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨2,0,6⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{2}}=⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨0,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(-1,3,-9)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${Q}_{1}(3,-1,11)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${Q}_{1}(4,2,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(1,0,2)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${Q}_{1}(6,2,2)$ and ${Q}_{2}(1,0,-2)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(3,-2,3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-2,1,2⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩)-⟨3,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,t,\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=3,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =3 \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =3 \\\\ |⟨-2t,\\,t,\\,2t⟩| & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{(-2t)^{2}+{t}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{9{t}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\pm 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨3,-2,3⟩+⟨-2,1,2⟩=⟨1,-1,5⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨3,-2,3⟩-⟨-2,1,2⟩=⟨5,-3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c73d23bd8bda3653a2c735d25fd3f39c83e31fe3e1d881dcf365dcf8cc58b635" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${A}_{1}(-1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,-3,-1)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${A}_{1}(1,-1,-5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,3,2)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r