ourse_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(5,0,4)$ and $Q(-3,1,5).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ a \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6ec74c8d713ea023b21b4557edf499e22c8c80eb1d930a4730d1dab613f951b" "basis" 1493 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+1+1=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" 