ttribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $A$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=a+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $a$ is the position vector of $A.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $A(4,5,3)$ and $B(-1,2,0)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩-⟨4,5,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-35973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-35973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-35973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-35973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $K(-4,-3,-1)$ and $L(1,2,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $K$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=k+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $k$ is the position vector of $K.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $K(-4,-3,-1)$ and $L(1,2,4),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{KL} \\\\  & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨-4,-3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-69772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(2,3,6)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-3,-2,1⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=\\sqrt{14}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨2,3,6⟩+t⟨-3,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨2,3,6⟩+t⟨-3,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨2,3,6⟩+t⟨-3,-2,1⟩)-⟨2,3,6⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-3,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3t,\\,-2t,\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=\\sqrt{14},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ |⟨-3t,\\,-2t,\\,t⟩| & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\sqrt{(-3t)^{2}+(-2t)^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\pm t\\sqrt{14} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨2,3,6⟩+⟨-3,-2,1⟩=⟨-1,1,7⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨2,3,6⟩-⟨-3,-2,1⟩=⟨5,5,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(-1,1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-126995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${A}_{1}(-1,-1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-5,5)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(-1,1,-7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(-1,1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(1,-1,-7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(1,1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-5,5)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${A}_{1}(-1,1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-69783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,0,0)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ Find all the possible points $R$ on that line such that $RP=3\\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-69783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $R$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩)-⟨1,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,t,\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PR=3\\sqrt{3},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RP & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PR}| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,t,\\,t⟩| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\pm t\\sqrt{3} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 3$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{R}_{1}}=⟨1,0,0⟩+3⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨4,3,3⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{R}_{2}}=⟨1,0,0⟩-3⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨-2,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${R}_{1}(4,3,3)$ and ${R}_{2}(-2,-3,-3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-69783" "field" nil