7443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $Q$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩)-⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨1,-1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+(-t)^{2}+(5t)^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{27{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\pm 3\\sqrt{3}t & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{1}}=⟨1,1,1⟩+⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨2,0,6⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{2}}=⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨0,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(-1,3,-9)$"] ["text" "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$"] ["text" "${Q}_{1}(3,-1,11)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$"] ["text" "${Q}_{1}(4,2,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(1,0,2)$"] ["text" "${Q}_{1}(6,2,2)$ and ${Q}_{2}(1,0,-2)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-77443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(3,-2,3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-2,1,2⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩)-⟨3,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,t,\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=3,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =3 \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =3 \\\\ |⟨-2t,\\,t,\\,2t⟩| & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{(-2t)^{2}+{t}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{9{t}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\pm 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨3,-2,3⟩+⟨-2,1,2⟩=⟨1,-1,5⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨3,-2,3⟩-⟨-2,1,2⟩=⟨5,-3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${A}_{1}(-1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,-3,-1)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(1,-1,-5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,3,2)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-3,1)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(1,1,-5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,3,2)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(1,2,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(-5,3,1)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${A}_{1}(1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-3,1)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(3,1,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-1,0,2⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=\\sqrt{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩)-⟨3,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-1,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=\\sqrt{5},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |⟨-t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{(-t)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+0+4{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\pm \\sqrt{5}t & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨3,1,1⟩+⟨-1,0,2⟩=⟨2,1,3⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨3,1,1⟩-⟨-1,0,2⟩=⟨4,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-126991" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126991" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${A}_{1}(1,2,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(2,1,-2)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,1)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,2,-1)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,-1,1)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-126991" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-3,5,0)$ and $Q(0,-3,2).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(-3)+2+0=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-162167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below gives a parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(4,3,5)$ and $Q(6,3,1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=(2t+4)\\,i+a\\,j+b\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(6\\,i+3\\,j+k)-(4\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\,i-4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=(4\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k)+t(2\\,i-4\\,k)\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(4\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k)+t(2\\,i-4\\,k) \\\\  & =(2t+4)\\,i+3\\,j+(5-4t)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=3+(5-4t)+1=9-4t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-162191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10-2t"] ["math" "2t+8"] ["math" "4t"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "9-4t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9-4t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(0,-2,2)$ and $Q(1,-1,1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ b \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+0=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-162165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(5,0,4)$ and $Q(-3,1,5).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ a \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+1+1=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below gives a parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,-1,1)$ and $Q(2,-3,0).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=a\\,i-(2t+1)\\,j+b\\,k,\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(2\\,i-3\\,j)-(i-j+k) \\\\  & =i-2\\,j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=(i-j+k)+t(i-2\\,j-k)\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(i-j+k)+t(i-2\\,j-k) \\\\  & =(t+1)\\,i-(2t+1)\\,j+(1-t)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(t+1)+(1-t)+0=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d4aa45eff4688d5db2e903a0785eccff8ba8ea57ae78058a7e274d455c59811b"} {"question" "q-162189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4t"] ["math" "1-4t"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3t+2"] ["math" "t+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "q-162189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab64f97af3f5a9f65f4f02ce5e9cc0cb75986bac92ada0bda3cc81f6df879178"} {"question" "e-12442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(3,-1,7)$ and parallel to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/assets/48f9afd751f6424fe465e494fd254593de065563231a1f5df07741789969c1af.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/example-12442.json" "file_sha256" "56941c27da1e3087bcae3f0283707684bfa76b8c065be6e7259ae50753d31238"} {"question" "e-12442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of $P$.\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/assets/9264ecd5e62e51eec08ae686461f8b3d99aadbddd2363b5c700c72839d59524f.png)\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/example-12442.json" "file_sha256" "56941c27da1e3087bcae3f0283707684bfa76b8c065be6e7259ae50753d31238"} {"question" "e-12443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $P(1,-1,2)$ and $Q(3,2,7).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/example-12443.json" "file_sha256" "4fef85780406edafa6b93ab680712a30837bdc0f8978c198a9367887bc142be9"} {"question" "e-12443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of $P.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $P(1,-1,2)$ and $Q(3,2,7),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =⟨3,2,7⟩-⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,3,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/example-12443.json" "file_sha256" "4fef85780406edafa6b93ab680712a30837bdc0f8978c198a9367887bc142be9"} {"question" "e-12444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,2,0)$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}= \\langle -4,1,1 \\rangle.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $PA=6\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/example-12444.json" "file_sha256" "978d82717b86045638dc7b7923b8656369bbd718c5a4e360f50f3279a9df67af"} {"question" "e-12444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,2,0⟩+t⟨-4,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\langle 1, 2, 0 \\rangle + t \\langle -4, 1, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,2,0⟩+t⟨-4,1,1⟩)-⟨1,2,0⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-4,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4t,\\,t,\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=6\\sqrt{2},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PA & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ |⟨-4t,\\,t,\\,t⟩| & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{(-4t)^{2}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{18{t}^{2}} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\pm 3t\\sqrt{2} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ t & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 2$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨1,2,0⟩+2⟨-4,1,1⟩=⟨-7,4,2⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨1,2,0⟩-2⟨-4,1,1⟩=⟨9,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are $A_1(-7, 4, 2)$ and $A_2(9, 0, -2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/example-12444.json" "file_sha256" "978d82717b86045638dc7b7923b8656369bbd718c5a4e360f50f3279a9df67af"} {"question" "e-12445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Using $\\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j},\\mathbf{k}$ notation, find a parametrization of the line segment $\\overline{PQ},$ where $P(-4,1,2)$ and $Q(-2,5,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/example-12445.json" "file_sha256" "10aa9852e0f7f78b56e3e0838068cda32115346326765f11219a2c090e9edf27"} {"question" "e-12445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(-2\\,i+5\\,j-k)-(-4\\,i+j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v} \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\mathbf{r} = (-4 \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}) + t (2 \\, \\mathbf{i} + 4 \\, \\mathbf{j} - 3 \\, \\mathbf{k})\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(-4\\,i+j+2\\,k)+t(2\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k) \\\\  & =(2t-4)\\,i+(4t+1)\\,j+(2-3t)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/example-12445.json" "file_sha256" "10aa9852e0f7f78b56e3e0838068cda32115346326765f11219a2c090e9edf27"} {"question" "q-35966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "801d5209337e023ff3d224a8b673221fb723d5838d61cb4e464213e43818b7f7" "reviewer_session" "01a108cd-e7f4-73f3-b8fc-c82135bc6b7d" "rationale" "A line through P=(−1,−4,5) parallel to v=(1,0,−1) is r=P+tv for every real t, exactly original option 1. The complete saved choices, authentic worked solution, and Correct grade confirm it. The database key has identical vectors, parameter placement, and parameter 